I'm just trying to print the location of the UAV (Latitude, Longitude, Altitude). After setting the update rate, I call my callback function as so:
`telemetry->subscribe_position(PositionCallbackFunc);`

```
void PositionCallbackFunc(Telemetry::Position position)
{
    gDronePosition.alt = position.absolute_altitude_m;
    gDronePosition.lat = position.latitude_deg;
    gDronePosition.lon = position.longitude_deg;
    std::cout<< "Reported Drone Position: \r\n";
    std::cout << "Altitude: " << position.relative_altitude_m << " m" << std::endl
              << "Latitude: " << position.latitude_deg << std::endl
              << "Longitude: " << position.longitude_deg << std::endl;

 
    std::chrono::time_point<std::chrono::system_clock> now = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
    auto duration = now.time_since_epoch();
    m_drone_pos_update_Time = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(duration).count();
}
```

It never seems to enter the Callback function, and when I try to print the altitude latitude and longitude values they print as "nan"

